  "notes": "Modified cash basis village. Governmental lines from the governmental funds statement Total Governmental Funds column (p5); its Total column prints transfers only as the net (12,000), recorded as transfers_out (fund columns: Street +13,114, Sales Tax -25,114). Business-type lines from the modified cash basis proprietary funds statement Total column (p7), incl. nonoperating grant, capital outlay, loan principal and interest; it ties to the government-wide figures (beginning 339,634, ending 352,449). The Statement of Activities (p2) presents Water differently (expenses 95,791, charges 83,317, operating grants 10,500: grant 10,000 netted). Cash: governmental funds balance sheet cash and cash equivalents 273,091 (ending_cash), certificates of deposit 59,954 (ending_investments), county treasurer cash 3,083 printed separately; beginning cash not printed (null). Detail: General Fund from the departmental combining statement (p13, more detailed; the General Fund budget schedule p10 is not recorded to avoid double counting; its Police protection 16,500 identifies the Interlocal agreements line as public safety); Street and Sales Tax Fund budget schedules (pp11-12); proprietary statement-column detail not recorded (aligned with FY2024: other funds have their own schedules; proprietary cash flows not recorded, cash basis); the Keno Fund has no schedule and is not in detail. Read pages 1-13 of 13"
